  "scope": "C/Rust debug and plain q35/KVM SMP2 kernels each pass48 combined (39core+9BRD), then39 isolated core. All14 completion,10 swait and13 generic wait definitions selected exactly once; scheduler-text placement retained.",
  "diagnostics": "No compiler/objtool or rejected runtime diagnostics and no required skips. Debug instrumentation and plain exclusions resolve exactly; BUG=y in both.",
  "new_coverage": "Four cases cover priority-prefix/ordinary-LIFO/exclusive-tail and field preservation, EBUSY changed flags/untouched NULL links and first-node-only rejection, linked/selflinked poisoning and re-addition, ordinary-spin constructor static class/name/LD_WAIT_CONFIG plus null-unused nondebug arguments and IRQ restoration. Structural snapshots and callback order independently observed.",
  "remaining_C": "Prepare/finish policy, callbacks, prelock/mixed flags access, spinlock/lockdep and list/state/LKMM adapters, scheduler and macros.",
  "limitations": "No actual blocked wait_event/wait-bit handoff, POLLFREE race, CFI/modules/arm64/performance proof. Synthetic retirement from prior tests remains uninstrumented.",
